{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530662-v20-mortal-definition","id":1530662,"title":"V20 Mortal definition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-12T12:11:41-08:00","id":1530662,"title":"V20 Mortal definition","content":"Do Hunters, Ghouls or Mages count as mortals for purposes of merits, flaws and disciplines?<br /> <br /> For example the <b>Kiss of Death </b>flaw (The Black Hand A Guide to the TalMaheRa p.179) mentions that the effect applies only to exanguinated mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T15:47:11-08:00","id":1530675,"title":"","content":"Hunters definitely count as mortals, though if they're also Imbued, they're specifically resistant to a lot of mortal-only effects that Vampires have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T16:18:40-08:00","id":1530683,"title":"","content":"Ultimately V20 (like all the editions before it) are very bad at defining a line here. A lot of this is just the legacy of VtM being first, and having designs going back to 1991 that didn't know what the other supernatural critters would look like mechanically in order to have a clear mechanical delineation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T02:38:28-08:00","id":1530725,"title":"","content":"In my opinion mortals are all living being without any super ability at all. For Vampires rules, werewolves and mages does not count as mortal.<br /> <br /> There's some exception, from my understanding ghouls are still mortals, they're just stronger thanks to vitae. Sorcerer and hunters are still mortal too, even if they posess supernaturals abilities.<br /> It's not really clear why those are and not the other, as heavy arms said the books don't define a specific line or reason. It's up to the ST to create that line if they need to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 02-16-2024, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}